{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"# INVESTIGATION (session cd66bacc) — why the loop survives six layers of fixes, and the step-back design\n\n## The accreted control stack (verified on main @065af7c163)\n\nComposition order in agent_call.build_agent_kwargs (innermost to outermost): step-limit steering, memoization, completion evidence policy, runaway guard. Six shipped mitigations: criteria-scaled step floor (completion.py::verify_step_floor), path-normalized read_file memo + graduated nudges (agent_call._memo_toolsets, lever 2 of epic 10ae), one-governed-action-per-response + 3-unique-evidence-responses-per-criterion boundary (completion_tool_policy.py), runaway distinct-ratio abort (agent_call._runaway_guard_toolsets), banked incremental verdicts + batched successor recovery + deterministic finalizer (workflow/completion_recovery.py, completion_banking.py), and file_impact prefetch (workflow/completion_prefetch.py).\n\n## Two architectural defects the layers cannot fix\n\n**(1) The runaway guard counts memo-served repeats as loop evidence.** The guard is OUTERMOST: its call_tool appends the signature and computes the trip ratio BEFORE delegating to the memo layer (agent_call.py `_runaway_guard_toolsets` vs `_memo_toolsets`). So a re-read that lever 2 made FREE (served by slicing the path cache, zero repo round-trip) still fills the guard window and trips RunawayToolLoopError. Lever 2 and the guard fight each other: the run in this bug's repro died at distinct_ratio_window=0.5 with read_file:a0cce810 x13 — those 13 were mostly memo hits costing nothing except guard budget. The 2000-line read window (pai_tools._READ_MAX_LINES) means the 445-line architecture.md fits in ONE read; the re-requests are pure model behavior the guard punishes instead of the memo absorbing.\n\n**(2) The finite-evidence boundary manufactures FALSE met=false.** completion_tool_policy.BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE banks met=false after three unique evidence responses — its own module header admits \"a persistently batching model can bank met=false against a file that exists\". A thorough-but-inefficient model therefore converts infrastructure friction into a substantive FAIL verdict, which is exactly the false-negative shape observed in the akitainu close (criteria \"unmet — evidence present but not reached\"). Fail-closed here is the wrong polarity: search exhaustion is EPISTEMIC (unknown), not substantive (unmet).\n\nRoot diagnosis: every fix adds another IN-BAND control (nudges, steering notices, synthetic results) to an open-ended tool loop, and the controls now conflict. The verdict's reliability is hostage to emergent model search behavior that no budget/guard tuning can bound.\n\n## Step-back design — make the loop impossible instead of policing it\n\nInvert the architecture: **deterministic evidence compilation + tool-free judgment**.\n\n1. **Deterministic per-criterion dossiers (no agent).** Extend completion_prefetch from \"assistance\" to the PRIMARY evidence channel: for each banked-unverified criterion, compile file_impact contents, referencing-commit diffs, verify_commands output, and ticket comments into a bounded dossier (rank/skeleton-compress exactly as prefetch does today).\n2. **Tool-FREE judgment calls.** Judge criteria in batches with structured output only — the model receives dossiers and returns per-criterion verdicts. No tools means no tool loop: no runaway guard, no memo, no step budget; cost is O(criteria), deterministic, cacheable.\n3. **Declarative gap-fill, bounded at K rounds.** A judge may return needs_evidence [{path, line_range | symbol | grep}] instead of a verdict; the DETERMINISTIC layer fetches exactly that and re-asks. K=2 rounds; requests are data, not tool calls, so they cannot loop.\n4. **Honest tri-state banking.** met / unmet / insufficient_evidence. NEVER bank met=false at a search boundary. insufficient_evidence surfaces as an actionable finding naming the missing evidence and leaves the bank entry re-checkable; met/unmet stay banked across runs (existing tree-sha stamps).\n5. **Agentic fallback becomes opt-in** (config), only for criteria the dossier layer marks un-compilable; it keeps the existing guards. Also fix defect (1) regardless: the guard must count only calls that MISS the memo (observe executed work, not model chatter) — a composition change (guard inside memo) that removes the layer conflict for every agentic gate, not just completion.\n\nMigration: (a) land the guard/memo composition fix + tri-state banking (small, kills the worst false-negatives); (b) land dossier + tool-free judgment behind verify config; (c) flip the default; agentic loop demoted to fallback. Each step independently shippable and testable against the akitainu-shaped fixture named in this ticket's AC."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786681419955850001,"uuid":"2e3f008b-cec6-4a34-b6d6-4c8a16fc54ab"}